# Vercel deploys the FRONTEND only.
#
# The backend cannot run on Vercel's serverless runtime:
#   * its dependencies total ~223 MB installed (OpenCV alone is 118 MB)
#     against a 250 MB unzipped function limit, before any models
#   * the ONNX models add roughly 90 MB more
#   * SQLite needs a writable, persistent disk; Vercel's filesystem is
#     read-only apart from an ephemeral /tmp
#   * video analysis can exceed the function execution timeout
#
# Excluding it here also stops Vercel's Python builder from detecting
# backend/main.py and failing with "No FastAPI entrypoint found".
#
# To run the full system, use START.bat locally, or host the backend on a
# platform with persistent disk and a larger image budget (Render, Railway,
# Fly.io) and point VITE_API_BASE at it.

backend/
training/
notebooks/
tools/
brand/

.venv/
.tmp/
.pipcache/
.npmcache/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

requirements.txt
START.bat
*.ipynb
